{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02133",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.09,
      "end_seconds": 2.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Morning, come on through."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 3.78,
      "end_seconds": 9.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "Hi doctor, I got here as fast as I could."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 10.42,
      "end_seconds": 14.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.9,
      "end_seconds": 27.03,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "So, please do. Extra information is always welcome. Did you take the bus in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.69,
      "end_seconds": 32.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "I drove. The roads were quiet today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.01,
      "end_seconds": 37.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "So what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.67,
      "end_seconds": 49.55,
      "duration_seconds": 6.88,
      "text": "I wanted to get a chronic cough with lots of phlegm looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.59,
      "end_seconds": 54.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.59,
      "end_seconds": 60.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "Around three days... no wait, it's more like two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.36,
      "end_seconds": 71.88,
      "duration_seconds": 9.52,
      "text": "Alright, can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.57,
      "end_seconds": 80.42,
      "duration_seconds": 6.85,
      "text": "Yes, mornings. That makes it worse. It's mild, honestly. I'd say on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.42,
      "end_seconds": 84.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.05,
      "end_seconds": 95.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Let me think, it usually comes with tiredness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.65,
      "end_seconds": 102.36,
      "duration_seconds": 6.71,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 102.46,
      "end_seconds": 108.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.67,
      "end_seconds": 112.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.36,
      "end_seconds": 117.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "That's fine, one at a time. I'll ask about everything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.16,
      "end_seconds": 123.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "The tiredness? That's been for about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.48,
      "end_seconds": 132.9,
      "duration_seconds": 7.42,
      "text": "Have you had a chronic cough with lots of phlegm before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.7,
      "end_seconds": 141.27,
      "duration_seconds": 7.57,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened last winter, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.15,
      "end_seconds": 146.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Alright, a few quick ones: chest pain or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.01,
      "end_seconds": 157.66,
      "duration_seconds": 10.65,
      "text": "No, no chest pain, no weight loss. I was getting out of breath at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.98,
      "end_seconds": 161.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Any fever or coughing up blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.56,
      "end_seconds": 164.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.42,
      "end_seconds": 167.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.63,
      "end_seconds": 172.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "That's normal as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.45,
      "end_seconds": 177.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.32,
      "end_seconds": 184.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "My mother has an underactive thyroid. My mother had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.27,
      "end_seconds": 188.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.84,
      "end_seconds": 193.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Just my womb taken out, fifteen years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.2,
      "end_seconds": 212.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.78,
      "end_seconds": 215.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "I have diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.81,
      "end_seconds": 216.51,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Ah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.59,
      "end_seconds": 224.36,
      "duration_seconds": 6.77,
      "text": "Yes, heart disease. I've had eczema, yes. Anxiety, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.91,
      "end_seconds": 230.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.06,
      "end_seconds": 242.88,
      "duration_seconds": 10.82,
      "text": "Yeah, I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.88,
      "end_seconds": 245.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.28,
      "end_seconds": 252.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.55,
      "end_seconds": 255.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Okay, how about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.96,
      "end_seconds": 260.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "No, I've never smoked in my life."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.83,
      "end_seconds": 265.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Okay, tell me about your eating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.06,
      "end_seconds": 272.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.51,
      "end_seconds": 277.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.16,
      "end_seconds": 286.57,
      "duration_seconds": 7.41,
      "text": "So, it's something called glic... gliclazide, 80 milligrams, maybe, twice a day for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.19,
      "end_seconds": 292.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Do you have the packet or the prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 294.97,
      "end_seconds": 304.09,
      "duration_seconds": 9.12,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. Aspirin, 75 milligrams, once a day. Hydrocortisone cream, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.33,
      "end_seconds": 305.31,
      "duration_seconds": 0.98,
      "text": "Mm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.13,
      "end_seconds": 314.37,
      "duration_seconds": 7.24,
      "text": "It's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a round yellow one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.41,
      "end_seconds": 322.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.87,
      "end_seconds": 339.2,
      "duration_seconds": 14.33,
      "text": "For the anxiety, I believe. My wife sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. I'd been on glimepiride, not any more though, I stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.44,
      "end_seconds": 343.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Let's start with the basic checks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.27,
      "end_seconds": 358.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 378.55,
      "end_seconds": 393.04,
      "duration_seconds": 14.49,
      "text": "Okay: height 153 centimetres, respiratory rate 14. And weight 94 kilos, BP is 109 over 73, temp 36.8 degrees, heart rate 73, SpO2 99 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 394.33,
      "end_seconds": 398.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 399.41,
      "end_seconds": 400.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "Let me feel here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 413.14,
      "end_seconds": 418.72,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "There are coarse crackles at both bases and the fingers are slightly clubbed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 423.46,
      "end_seconds": 435.4,
      "duration_seconds": 11.94,
      "text": "You can relax now. So, based on the history and the examination, I'd lean towards a flare of bronchiectasis. I'd also keep a chest infection in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 451.25,
      "end_seconds": 489.48,
      "duration_seconds": 38.23,
      "text": "I think a chest X-ray makes sense here, for bronchiectasis flare. A sputum culture is what I'd like next, for purulent sputum. Let's use clarithromycin, 500 milligrams, twice a day, fourteen days. That's for bronchiectasis flare. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. Keep up your airway clearance exercises twice a day. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 490.45,
      "end_seconds": 491.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 492.6,
      "end_seconds": 499.9,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "Let's review you in two weeks. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 501.79,
      "end_seconds": 504.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}